## 💡 Learning

I learned that the model does not simply copy the driving video. It extracts motion information, detects keypoints, and transfers the motion to the source image. The source image provides appearance, while the driving sequence provides motion.

## 📌 SOFTWARE ENGINEERING REQUIREMENT — WEEK 5

### Activity Diagram — Complete Animation Pipeline

The diagram describes input preparation, model loading, motion transfer, and output-video creation.

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A([Start]) --> B[Select Source Image]
    B --> C[Convert Image to RGB]
    C --> D[Crop and Resize to 256x256]

    E[Select Driving Video] --> F[Read Video Frames]
    F --> G[Extract FPS]
    G --> H[Resize Frames to 256x256]

    D --> I[Load Model Configuration]
    H --> I
    I --> J[Load Pretrained Checkpoint]
    J --> K[Load Generator]
    J --> L[Load Keypoint Detector]
    K --> M[Make Animation]
    L --> M
    M --> N[Extract Motion]
    N --> O[Transfer Motion to Source Image]
    O --> P[Generate Frames]
    P --> Q[Create Output Video]
    Q --> R([End])
```